 could all stack on top of each  other  in a sort of ramp-like configuration and  allow some of the turtles at the top to  climb out  and be freed the turtle shared this idea  with the bale  and after some convincing everyone was  on board  now with the insight that having  offspring could help solve their problem  and alleviate their suffering the  turtles began reproducing intentionally  with this in mind  birthing new turtles into the pit on  purpose  as soon as the bale had enough offspring  and the offspring matured to large  enough size  the turtles all stacked on each other in  a sort of a skew ramp configuration  all the way up to the top of the wall  for the first time  several turtles made their way out of  the pit and into the beyond  above it following these several turtles  climbing out however  the remaining turtles would soon find  themselves without enough turtles left  to climb high enough  and so they all climbed back down into  the pit again  now knowing that the process worked  though they began birthing more  offspring with the intention of freeing  more of themselves  a system of sorts was established and  embraced wherein  the eldest turtles would be the ones  designated to leave first  in order of their age leaving the  remaining younger turtles to wait their  turn  and continue reproducing occasionally  there were also certain younger turtles  who  through either force perceived  importance flukes in the system  persuasion or all of the above made  their way out  sometime earlier in general the cycle of  the system would be accepted and  repeated over and over  generation after generation more  offspring brought into the pit  only to work the first two thirds of  their life to survive and hope that they  would make it into the eldest position  and finally climb out finally find their  reason and pay out for it all  finally become a member of their bale  who made it finally touch some state of  freedom  ultimately throughout the whole process  almost every turtle was born  in some sense to help solve their  parents problem their parents problem  becoming theirs  the new turtles eventually becoming  compelled to birth more offspring  to help solve what now became their  problem and then repeat  a part of a later generation one turtle  in particular  who was not particularly unique at all  and in fact was like many others in its  view  often found itself questioning was it  all worth the hassle  was the measure of pain worth the  potential pleasure of the payoff  was everything worth the trouble of  being born  it wondered and struggled with these  questions which ultimately made it  question whether it should participate  in the whole system  was it fair to birth more turtles to do  the same simply to potentially make  things better for itself  in hopes that its offspring would find  this agreeable  of course this turtle was aware that  some turtles found value in the whole  thing  meaning in the pit the pursuit of  getting out and the occasional pleasures  along the way  but this particular turtle found these  other turtles to be delusional  at best it only envied them knowing that  it could never really see its life this  way  and find sufficient justification in the  suffering  ultimately this turtle realized only the  individual could decide  for themselves if it was better or worse  to have been born into the pit or not  but it also realized that the paradox  was that the individual could only  decide once they were born  and it was too late not to be  to this day the turtles continue on in  the pit some ignoring this issue  some unaware some struggling or in  revolt with it  in some distance of some future perhaps  the turtles will figure out a way for an  ultimate and total escape of their  entire population  and hopefully for their sake outside the  pit  is what they've hoped for but for now  the general suffering  it's turtles all the way down  [Music]  as mentioned at the beginning of the  vide